          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong one-parameter group
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operators"} unitary operators
            in a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism+of+groups"} homomorphism of groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R} \to U(H),
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U%28H%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(H)
            denotes its group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operators"} unitary operators
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/addition"} additive
            group of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          %p
            More generally, one can define
            %strong
              one-parameter
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroups"} semigroups
            of operators in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+space"} Banach space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as homomomorphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}_{\ge0} \to B(X),
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(X)
            denotes the semigroup of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operators"} bounded operators
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X
          %p
            Typically, we also require a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuity
            condition such as continuity in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+topology"} strong topology
          %h2#stone_theorem Stone theorem
          %p
            Strongly continuous one-parameter unitary groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U_t)_{t\ge0}
            of operators in a Hilbert space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            are in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-adjoint+operator"} self-adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unbounded+operators"} unbounded operators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          %p This bijection sends
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi itA
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A
                  \\mapsto
                  \\big(
                  t\mapsto \exp(itA)
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operator"} bounded
            if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is norm-continuous.
          %h2#hilleyosida_theorem Hille–Yosida theorem
          %p
            Strongly continuous one-parameter semigroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of bounded operators on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+space"} Banach space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (alias
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
                \-semigroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo ≤
